51: /// # Safety
52: ///
53: /// Implementations of `read` must validate every requested physical extent
54: /// against ACPI table memory-map metadata before reading it. `read_rsdp` may
55: /// additionally support the bounded legacy x86 reserved firmware window for
56: /// the RSDP itself; it must not extend that exception to root or child tables.
57: /// Both methods must copy only from checked, read-only, non-executable mappings,
58: /// ensure the complete extent is readable, and initialize all of `output` before
59: /// returning `Ok`. This module never creates mappings or dereferences physical
60: /// addresses itself.
