1: //! Bounded single-producer/single-consumer input queues for device IRQ paths.
2: //!
3: //! Each queue has one producer (its device IRQ handler) and one consumer on the
4: //! bootstrap CPU. Producers never wait or allocate; full queues drop the newest
5: //! byte and increment a saturating overflow counter.
